d result in minor flooding across the southern San Juan\nfoothills and communities further downstream.\n\nRivers have responded rapidly to recent rainfall due to saturated\nsoils and increased runoff potential. Thus, prolonged periods of\nadditional rainfall over these regions would trigger a similar\nresponse. The current precipitation forecast suggests larger peaks in\nseveral creeks and rivers than what has been observed over the\nprevious 7 days. However, high end probabilistic rainfall amounts\n(i.e. above 90th percentile) may lead to rivers exceeding action\nstage to minor flooding. Most probable basins to see significant\nrises include; the Rio Blanco, San Juan, Piedra, Los Pinos/Vallecito\nCreek, and the Animas River Basins.\n\nConvective storms and periods of heavy rainfall fed from said\ntropical moisture could result in localized flooding impacts across\nthe CWA, however, confidence decreases rapidly north of the San\nJuans. Please continue to monitor the forecast as these systems\nevolve. Especially for those who reside and/or plan to recreate in\nthe southwest quadrant of the forecast area.","ends":"2026-09-30T06:00:00-06:00","severity":"Unknown","areaDesc":"Archuleta, CO; Dolores, CO; Gunnison, CO; Hinsdale, CO; La Plata, CO; Montezuma, CO; Ouray, CO; San Juan, CO; San Miguel, CO; Grand, UT; San Juan, UT","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.ce67801ec73048f07c44dd0418c6a50edd1c8fdc.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.ce67801ec73048f07c44dd0418c6a50edd1c8fdc.001.1"}],"afd":{"office":"GJT","issued":"2026-09-26T18:46:00+00:00","snippet":"000 FXUS65 KGJT 261846 AFDGJT Area Forecast Discussion National Weather Service Grand Junction CO 1246 PM MDT Sat Sep 26 2026 .KEY MESSAGES... - Warmer and drier conditions over the weekend. - Another push of moisture will arrive by Monday, bringing widespread moderate to heavy precipitation through midweek. && .DISCUSSION... Issued at 1245 PM MDT Sat Sep 26 2026 PREDOMINATELY DRY THIS WEEKEND: A ","url":"https://forecast.weather.gov/product.php?site=GJT&issuedby=GJT&product=AFD&format=CI"},"hwo":null,"fwf":{"office":"GJT","issued":"2026-09-26T19:20:00+00:00","snippet":".DISCUSSION...There are a few isolated thunderstorms across the region over the higher terrain this afternoon, but otherwise expect mostly quiet conditions today and tomorrow with temperatures near normal to five degrees above normal. Cooler wet weather moves into the region Monday through mid week and dries out for the end of the week. Critical fire weather conditions are not expected. ...GUSTY E","url":"https://forecast.weather.gov/product.php?site=GJT&issuedby=GJT&product=FWF&format=CI"},"coagmet":null,"aviation":{"icao":"KTEX","distance_km":14.9,"raw_metar":"METAR KTEX 262155Z AUTO 27007KT 10SM OVC080 15/05 A3040 RMK AO2","temp_f":59,"wind_dir":270,"wind_kt":7,"gust_kt":null,"visibility":"10+","cover":"OVC","flight_category":"VFR","altimeter":1029.5,"observed":1790459700,"raw_taf":"TAF KTEX 261720Z 2618/2718 26006KT P6SM FEW250 FM270300 14003KT P6SM SCT250","url":"https://aviationweather.gov/data/metar/?ids=KTEX&hours=0"},"airgradient":null,"airnow":{"aqi":13,"category":"Good","parameter":"PM2.5","reporting_area":"Telluride","observed":"2026-09-26 14","by_parameter":{"PM2.5":{"aqi":13,"category":"Good","reporting_area":"Telluride","observed":"2026-09-26 14"},"PM10":{"aqi":11,"category":"Good","reporting_area":"Telluride","observed":"2026-09-26 14"}},"url":"https://www.airnow.gov/","distance_km":6.5},"openmeteo_aq":{"pm25":1.5,"pm10":2.2,"co":101,"no2":0.2,"so2":0.2,"o3":98,"european_aqi":39,"us_aqi":39,"time":"2026-09-26T15:00"},"usgs":{"station_id":"09171240","station_name":"LAKE FORK SAN MIGUEL RV ABV TROUT LAKE NR OPHIR CO","distance_km":4.5,"discharge_cfs":30.7,"gauge_height_ft":2.74,"water_temp_f":null,"observed":"2026-09-26T15:15:00.000-06:00","url":"https://waterdata.usgs.gov/nwis/uv?site_no=09171240"},"snotel":{"station_name":"Lizard Head Pass","station_id":"586","distance_km":2.5,